#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/hiding-a-version.rst:2
msgid "How to hide a version and keep its documentation online"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/hiding-a-version.rst:4
msgid ""
"If you manage a project with a lot of versions, the version (flyout) menu"
" of your docs can be easily overwhelmed and hard to navigate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/hiding-a-version.rst:10
msgid "Overwhelmed flyout menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/hiding-a-version.rst:12
msgid ""
"You can deactivate the version to remove its docs, but removing its docs "
"isn't always an option. To not list a version in the flyout menu while "
"keeping its docs online, you can mark it as hidden. Go to your project's "
":menuselection:`Versions` tab, open the dot menu for the version, select "
":guilabel:`Configure version`, and toggle the :guilabel:`Hidden` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/hiding-a-version.rst:17
msgid ""
"Users that have a link to your old version will still be able to see your"
" docs. And new users can see all your versions (including hidden "
"versions) in the versions tab of your project at "
"``https://app.readthedocs.org/projects/<your-project>/versions/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/hiding-a-version.rst:20
msgid ""
"Check the docs about :ref:`versions' states <versions:Version States>` "
"for more information."
msgstr ""

